    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0413" n="343" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg343"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 182/19: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">
                        Colonel E. M. House to
                        the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-10T19:00:00+00:00"
                            >December 10, 1918—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your December 8, 5 p.m., serial number 149 [<hi rendition="#italic">152?</hi>]
                    from the Department, December 9, 9 p.m. [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a.m.?</hi>]<anchor n="20" xml:id="d335-f1"/> answering my 233.<anchor
                        n="21" xml:id="d335-f2"/> Secret for the President. After sending you my
                    number 233, I concluded that it would be best simply to advise Lord
                        Derby that I had communicated summary of these proceedings to
                    you. I have not committed you to any of the resolutions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d335-f1" n="20" xml:id="d335-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d335-f2" n="21" xml:id="d335-f2-content">
                <p>Forwarded to the Secretary of State as the Department’s No. 7, Dec. 7,. 1918, 11
                    a.m., <ref target="#pg340">p. 340</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
